>> title: Seven-Minute Eggs
>> category: Eggs
>> tags: eggs, boiled, jammy, topping, quick
>> counters: The Bowl Shop
>> aka: jammy eggs, soft-boiled eggs, seven minute egg, 7-minute egg, medium-boiled eggs, soft boiled egg, bowl egg
>> pairs-with: mujaddara, harissa
>> servings: 6
>> time: 20 min
>> slack: unforgiving — thirty seconds either side is a running yolk or a chalky ring, and there is no way back from either
>> step.1: boil 7 min from fridge-cold
>> step.2: ice bath 5 min
>> step.3: peel under the tap
>> step.4: halve and salt at the table

Lower @eggs{6%large}(300 g; straight from the fridge) into hard-boiling @water{2%qt}(1.9 L) on a spoon and ~boil{7%min}, keeping the water at a rolling boil the whole time.

Move @&(~1)boiled eggs{} straight into @ice water{1%qt}(950 mL) and ~cool{5%min}.

Crack @&(~1)chilled eggs{} all over on the counter and peel them under a running cold tap, starting at the fat end where the air pocket is.

Halve @&(~1)peeled eggs{} with a wet knife and season the cut faces with @flaky salt{1/2%tsp} and @black pepper{1/4%tsp}.
